WEBVTT

00:58.559 --> 00:59.393
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION

00:59.477 --> 01:00.978
CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED SAFELY
WITH SUPERVISION

02:18.722 --> 02:20.307
Is this how you always flirt?

02:24.436 --> 02:25.271
Are you insane?

02:48.002 --> 02:49.378
No way.

02:54.091 --> 02:55.217
It can't be, right?

02:57.052 --> 02:58.053
Why?

02:58.137 --> 03:01.223
Why does it feel like Mr. Kang
would put up with all my venting?

03:02.516 --> 03:03.809
Just one more drink together…

03:10.232 --> 03:12.151
Would you be up

03:14.111 --> 03:14.945
for a…

03:15.029 --> 03:16.322
Another drink at my place?

03:18.282 --> 03:19.617
No, you can't.

03:19.700 --> 03:21.201
Get it together, Cha Ji-yoon!

03:21.285 --> 03:25.164
For a drive? Do you live very far?

03:27.541 --> 03:29.752
No, I'm only five minutes away.

03:31.503 --> 03:32.338
Close one.

03:34.256 --> 03:35.341
Well, my place

03:35.424 --> 03:37.676
is right over there.

03:40.596 --> 03:41.513
Have a good night.

03:48.312 --> 03:50.439
Well done, Cha Ji-yoon. Nice save.

03:51.732 --> 03:53.233
Snapping out of it in the end

03:54.485 --> 03:57.529
is the best thing you did this year.

03:58.489 --> 04:01.575
Can't believe
I almost got involved with a superior.

04:02.868 --> 04:03.869
Gosh, that's horrifying.

04:04.662 --> 04:06.038
Absolutely horrifying.

04:06.121 --> 04:07.748
Alcohol really is my worst enemy.

04:07.831 --> 04:09.375
It gives me weird dreams too.

04:36.944 --> 04:39.989
Best thing I did, my ass!

04:44.159 --> 04:45.244
I can't go to work tomorrow.

04:55.212 --> 04:56.672
Are you free tomorrow?

04:56.755 --> 04:58.007
If you are,

04:58.090 --> 05:00.259
we should meet again.

05:00.884 --> 05:02.636
Would you be up…

05:04.680 --> 05:08.475
For a drive? Do you live very far?

05:09.560 --> 05:10.477
Have a good night.

05:16.608 --> 05:17.568
Was that a no?

05:38.213 --> 05:39.923
Buy two get one free? Yes please.

05:40.007 --> 05:41.300
BUTTER COCONUT BISCUIT

05:50.559 --> 05:51.727
Had a lot to drink last night?

05:51.810 --> 05:52.853
Yes.

05:57.691 --> 05:58.901
Oh, that's the stuff.

06:01.862 --> 06:03.197
That'll be 27,000 won.

06:03.280 --> 06:04.239
Give me a second.

06:09.078 --> 06:09.953
Hi.

06:10.913 --> 06:12.164
That'll be 1,800 won.

06:15.042 --> 06:16.085
Ms. Cha?

06:19.588 --> 06:20.464
Is this

06:21.173 --> 06:22.299
for real?

06:30.432 --> 06:32.726
I came out in a hurry, so…

06:39.483 --> 06:41.401
You've got a lot of snacks there.

06:41.485 --> 06:42.528
Oh, yes.

06:50.410 --> 06:51.578
Would you like an ice pop?

06:57.793 --> 07:00.003
If you don't like that one,
there's a chocolate--

07:18.105 --> 07:19.815
That'll be 31,200 won.

07:21.233 --> 07:23.735
Oh? He paid for this and didn't take it.

07:25.487 --> 07:27.739
-You know him, right?
-Sorry?

07:28.824 --> 07:29.658
Me?

07:55.893 --> 07:57.060
Mommy,

07:57.144 --> 07:59.438
that old lady's wearing undies like Dad's.

08:01.857 --> 08:04.818
What? No, these are silk pants
from Thailand.

08:04.902 --> 08:06.320
I'm sorry.

08:06.653 --> 08:07.487
Nice pants.

08:15.495 --> 08:17.247
Wait, he's laughing?

08:18.457 --> 08:19.625
Three-No-Man

08:20.334 --> 08:22.044
is laughing at me?

08:28.967 --> 08:30.260
I'm going to quit!

08:34.431 --> 08:40.103
EPISODE 2
DREAMING OF QUITTING, STILL CLOCKING IN!

08:45.108 --> 08:47.027
Even if he got fired,
he'll come in for a bit.

08:51.865 --> 08:55.369
What, are you going to say hi
as you hand this to him?

08:59.164 --> 09:01.833
This caller is unavailable.
You'll be redirected to voicemail.

09:04.127 --> 09:05.837
Your boyfriend's been pretty quiet lately.

09:06.505 --> 09:09.007
He used to call
like clockwork at lunchtime.

09:10.300 --> 09:12.261
He's like that
when he's too into an experiment.

09:12.636 --> 09:15.347
Geez, I hate even thinking
about experiments.

09:18.684 --> 09:20.894
No-ah, I'm going to run to the restroom.

09:21.645 --> 09:22.521
What?

09:28.986 --> 09:31.488
Bulgogi meal, nice.
Wow, looks like you took all the bulgogi.

09:32.155 --> 09:34.032
Enjoy your meal. You too.

09:34.741 --> 09:36.827
Why don't you ever eat with your own team?

09:36.910 --> 09:39.288
Hey now, I do this for a reason.

09:39.371 --> 09:42.040
He's always hunting for his next scoop
even while he's eating.

09:43.166 --> 09:44.501
The human grapevine in action.

09:45.127 --> 09:47.296
So, have you heard anything new lately?

09:47.379 --> 09:49.256
Still nothing more shocking
than Three-No-Man

09:49.339 --> 09:50.299
becoming our team lead.

09:51.008 --> 09:52.259
True.

09:52.342 --> 09:54.177
What's he like to work with?
Same as the rumors?

09:54.261 --> 09:57.222
Totally. No smile, no people, no sorry.
And he's the biggest workaholic

09:57.306 --> 09:58.515
I've ever seen.

09:59.224 --> 10:00.142
Does he not have a place yet?

10:00.434 --> 10:01.268
What do you mean?

10:01.351 --> 10:03.645
No one's ever seen him leaving the office.

10:03.729 --> 10:04.688
He's just always there,

10:05.439 --> 10:06.606
like built-in office furniture.

10:08.525 --> 10:10.610
The exact opposite of our team lead.

10:10.694 --> 10:12.863
We never see Mr. Ko stay at his desk.

10:13.697 --> 10:14.573
That reminds me.

10:15.657 --> 10:17.409
You know the backstory
on Mr. Kang and Mr. Ko?

10:17.909 --> 10:18.744
No.

10:19.411 --> 10:21.330
I heard this
through the Secretarial Team people.

10:22.164 --> 10:24.041
Mr. Kang used to be
on the Development Team,

10:24.124 --> 10:27.210
then briefly moved to the Planning Team
and worked under Mr. Ko.

10:27.294 --> 10:28.420
-Really?
-Yeah.

10:28.503 --> 10:30.630
Kang was still a Sr. Associate,
and get this,

10:30.714 --> 10:34.092
he actually reported his team lead,
Mr. Ko, for bribery,

10:35.135 --> 10:36.511
just so he could take that spot.

10:37.262 --> 10:38.096
What?

10:39.765 --> 10:42.184
So that's why Mr. Ko hates Mr. Kang.

10:42.851 --> 10:44.227
He really is the Grim Reaper.

10:44.311 --> 10:46.188
He's a sneaky one, for sure.

10:46.271 --> 10:47.105
Exactly.

10:48.565 --> 10:50.859
Hey, keep eating. Just keep eating.

10:52.319 --> 10:53.153
Mr. Kang?

10:53.904 --> 10:55.447
I thought he always eats alone.

11:05.499 --> 11:06.500
May I join you?

11:06.583 --> 11:07.584
Take this seat.

11:09.419 --> 11:10.670
-Right here.
-No.

11:26.937 --> 11:29.064
That is a severely unbalanced meal.

11:29.689 --> 11:31.233
You also drink a lot of instant coffee.

11:32.275 --> 11:33.235
That's bad for your health.

11:40.450 --> 11:42.536
I see you have no rice at all, Mr. Kang.

11:43.370 --> 11:45.789
No. I don't like putting on a gut.

12:00.011 --> 12:01.888
You get coffee after eating, correct?

12:02.764 --> 12:03.723
Coffee's on me today.

12:04.474 --> 12:05.308
Really?

12:05.809 --> 12:07.894
-You too, Ms. Cha.
-I have an urgent thing to do.

12:07.978 --> 12:09.354
But I completely forgot.

12:09.438 --> 12:11.148
Let me head back first.

12:15.652 --> 12:16.945
If you'll excuse me too.

12:21.533 --> 12:22.701
Ugh, that scared me.

12:23.243 --> 12:24.077
Me too.

12:24.161 --> 12:27.080
He always eats alone.
Why did he join us all of a sudden?

12:27.164 --> 12:28.665
And he kept trying to talk to you.

12:28.748 --> 12:29.833
I know, right?

12:31.626 --> 12:33.753
Iced Americano for me.

12:33.837 --> 12:35.130
What about you?

12:35.213 --> 12:36.339
I want

12:36.423 --> 12:38.133
a chocolate mocha smoothie.

12:38.758 --> 12:42.512
One iced Americano
and one chocolate mocha smoothie, please.

12:42.596 --> 12:43.513
Oh, no.

12:43.597 --> 12:45.140
It's my turn to pay this time.

12:46.057 --> 12:47.017
We'll pay with this card.

12:47.767 --> 12:48.685
Please tap it here.

12:48.768 --> 12:49.603
KANG SI-WOO

12:50.228 --> 12:52.063
I thought you had an urgent thing.

12:52.647 --> 12:53.607
I guess that was coffee.

12:54.900 --> 12:57.527
We desperately needed a caffeine fix.

12:57.986 --> 12:59.362
Then while you're getting caffeinated,

13:00.030 --> 13:01.198
shall we have a chat?

13:02.407 --> 13:04.159
I left something in the cafeteria.

13:04.242 --> 13:05.285
Can you get my coffee, No-ah?

13:06.578 --> 13:08.830
But you didn't bring anything
to the cafeteria.

13:13.960 --> 13:14.836
Thank you.

13:16.671 --> 13:17.923
What's going on?

13:20.258 --> 13:22.719
-What?
-You have something with Mr. Kang, right?

13:22.802 --> 13:24.721
What do you mean? There's nothing.

13:25.305 --> 13:26.431
He noticed too, didn't he?

13:26.515 --> 13:27.474
What?

13:27.557 --> 13:28.892
That you're great at your job.

13:28.975 --> 13:31.102
I bet he's trying to get you
to do some work for him.

13:31.770 --> 13:33.980
How could he? We're on different teams.

13:34.064 --> 13:36.358
Then what could it be?
Maybe he has a crush on you.

13:36.942 --> 13:38.235
That's even more unlikely.

13:38.318 --> 13:42.197
If that's not it either, then why is he
following you around like a puppy?

13:52.832 --> 13:54.543
Did you find the thing you lost?

13:54.626 --> 13:55.460
Yes.

13:56.169 --> 13:58.296
Also, are you free this evening?

13:58.380 --> 13:59.339
Yes.

13:59.422 --> 14:00.423
No!

14:00.507 --> 14:02.634
I've got plans I absolutely cannot cancel.

14:02.717 --> 14:03.927
I figured as much.

14:11.476 --> 14:13.979
See? He wants to see you after work.

14:14.062 --> 14:15.564
You know what it is?

14:15.647 --> 14:17.857
When someone accidentally
sees your embarrassing side,

14:17.941 --> 14:20.485
they start feeling
this one-sided sense of closeness to you.

14:20.986 --> 14:21.820
Sorry?

14:21.903 --> 14:24.281
He's just doing that
because he thinks I'm a pushover.

14:25.198 --> 14:26.324
Let's go.

14:37.294 --> 14:38.336
Hey!

14:38.420 --> 14:39.546
Lee Hye-ji!

14:40.297 --> 14:41.298
Lee Hye-ji!

14:41.381 --> 14:43.008
Gosh, how long has it been?

14:43.091 --> 14:44.926
Were you dying to see me?

14:45.010 --> 14:46.011
No way.

14:46.761 --> 14:49.514
Do you know how long it's been
since I've left the house by myself

14:49.598 --> 14:51.683
with a purse instead of a diaper bag?

14:52.475 --> 14:56.313
I'm going to eat all the spicy food
I wasn't allowed to eat

14:56.396 --> 14:57.814
while I was breastfeeding.

14:57.897 --> 14:58.940
Sounds good.

14:59.024 --> 15:00.317
Let's eat it all!

15:01.026 --> 15:02.861
It's this way.

15:02.944 --> 15:04.321
I'm so excited.

15:08.408 --> 15:11.161
Can you think of any reason
he wants to see you?

15:11.244 --> 15:12.329
I have no idea.

15:13.955 --> 15:15.832
Maybe he wants to make sure
I stay quiet before he quits.

15:16.249 --> 15:17.167
He's quitting?

15:17.542 --> 15:18.376
I think so.

15:18.460 --> 15:20.253
What do you mean, "stay quiet"?

15:20.670 --> 15:21.504
Well,

15:22.422 --> 15:25.842
I accidentally found out
a very private secret of his.

15:25.925 --> 15:27.218
So he got

15:27.969 --> 15:29.638
his very private secret exposed to you.

15:29.721 --> 15:30.764
Yeah.

15:30.847 --> 15:34.851
And he caught you in your private moment
looking like an absolute mess.

15:34.934 --> 15:36.853
-Yeah.
-And now he's quitting?

15:37.437 --> 15:38.647
That's the gist of it, yeah.

15:38.730 --> 15:41.524
You know, I think…

15:42.734 --> 15:43.985
he wants to ask you out.

15:44.611 --> 15:45.445
What?

15:45.528 --> 15:47.364
He laughed
when he saw you like that, right?

15:47.447 --> 15:49.324
And he's someone who never smiles.

15:49.407 --> 15:50.659
That can only mean

15:50.742 --> 15:52.535
that you made him

15:52.619 --> 15:54.245
let his guard down.

15:55.080 --> 15:56.915
And now that he's leaving the company,

15:57.415 --> 15:58.708
no need to worry about dating a colleague.

15:59.292 --> 16:00.794
He's going to ask you out.

16:00.877 --> 16:04.005
You're only saying that
because you don't know him.

16:04.089 --> 16:06.633
He's not the kind of person
to do such a thing at all.

16:07.217 --> 16:08.301
You know the type

16:08.385 --> 16:12.389
who always seem to have a dark cloud
over their head? He's like that.

16:12.472 --> 16:15.767
Still better than some idiot
prancing around all sunshine and flowers.

16:17.060 --> 16:18.436
Just go for it.

16:19.104 --> 16:21.147
You should feel each other out,

16:21.231 --> 16:22.816
if there's no major red flag.

16:23.316 --> 16:25.485
You get over a man
with another man, you know.

16:25.568 --> 16:26.778
You're wrong.

16:26.861 --> 16:30.156
You get over men with fried chicken
and beer and going to work.

16:30.240 --> 16:32.534
Come on, you can eat
and go to work together.

16:32.617 --> 16:33.868
How exciting is that?

16:34.452 --> 16:36.413
Stop talking nonsense and eat this.

16:37.080 --> 16:38.915
NEVER-DIE CHICKEN FEET

16:42.043 --> 16:43.044
Gosh, that's spicy.

16:45.422 --> 16:46.297
That burns.

16:58.893 --> 17:02.021
I see you took a little breather
this morning, Mr. Kang.

17:02.605 --> 17:03.732
Yes.

17:03.815 --> 17:06.067
The urgent work I had to deal with
has settled down for now.

17:07.193 --> 17:08.278
That's a relief.

17:09.779 --> 17:12.282
It looks like me coming in early

17:12.365 --> 17:13.992
was exhausting for you.

17:14.075 --> 17:15.952
No, how could I think that?

17:16.035 --> 17:18.997
-I always come to work on time, and…
-Doors opening.

17:19.080 --> 17:19.914
Hey, it's opening.

17:32.552 --> 17:33.386
Please, get in.

17:35.722 --> 17:38.516
You know, I think…

17:39.601 --> 17:40.727
he wants to ask you out.

17:41.895 --> 17:44.564
Oh, I left something
at the security checkpoint.

17:44.647 --> 17:45.565
Go ahead without me.

17:46.733 --> 17:48.568
Is it possible to leave stuff at security?

17:54.073 --> 17:55.033
Oh, man.

17:56.367 --> 17:58.286
Why did Hye-ji have to say
something like that?

17:59.204 --> 18:00.455
Now it's in my head.

18:04.501 --> 18:05.502
That kid's been a bit

18:06.711 --> 18:07.712
scatterbrained lately.

18:08.671 --> 18:11.257
Associate Jeon,
were you and Ms. Cha in the same intake?

18:11.341 --> 18:12.842
Yes. Oh, sorry.

18:13.885 --> 18:16.930
Ji-yoon was the first in our batch
to get promoted to Sr. Associate.

18:17.597 --> 18:20.058
Of course, I'm a little late too.

18:22.143 --> 18:24.813
You have lunch together as well.
Are you close?

18:25.396 --> 18:27.732
Yes, she's the one
I get along with the best in our batch.

18:29.734 --> 18:30.819
That's good.

18:31.402 --> 18:33.279
What do you mean?

18:51.798 --> 18:53.174
-Hey.
-Oh, hey.

18:53.258 --> 18:55.093
You started already? I told you to wait.

18:58.388 --> 18:59.264
Give me that.

19:04.269 --> 19:05.436
As you know,

19:06.312 --> 19:07.689
I didn't go to some fancy school,

19:08.314 --> 19:10.024
so I've had nobody opening doors for me.

19:10.108 --> 19:13.444
Exactly. That's why you're so impressive.

19:13.528 --> 19:16.698
You're doing great at work
without any of that.

19:18.867 --> 19:21.119
If I'm so great,
then why am I not a Sr. Associate yet?

19:22.287 --> 19:23.121
Hey.

19:23.830 --> 19:25.707
That's only because

19:25.790 --> 19:29.127
you've had terrible luck
with bosses so far.

19:30.128 --> 19:31.129
At this rate,

19:32.130 --> 19:33.423
I'm not sure I can

19:34.966 --> 19:36.092
raise Gyeol and Yul right.

19:36.175 --> 19:38.386
So what if you quit?

19:38.469 --> 19:42.181
You need to have another job lined up
before you make a move.

19:42.265 --> 19:43.141
Right.

19:44.893 --> 19:46.769
That's why I'm finding a new way in.

19:46.853 --> 19:47.687
Which one?

19:47.770 --> 19:48.813
He's here.

19:51.774 --> 19:53.401
My new lifeline.

19:57.363 --> 19:59.699
Fancy seeing you here.

19:59.782 --> 20:01.075
Oh, what's this?

20:01.159 --> 20:02.994
You two go ahead and talk.

20:03.077 --> 20:04.829
I need to take this call.

20:04.913 --> 20:06.539
My wife is calling right n--

20:06.623 --> 20:07.457
What are you doing?

20:07.540 --> 20:09.375
This is what friends are for.
Help me out. Please!

20:12.754 --> 20:14.088
Perfect timing.

20:21.721 --> 20:24.807
He even used my friend to meet me alone?

20:24.891 --> 20:26.726
It's surprisingly hard to get a moment

20:27.518 --> 20:28.728
for just the two of us.

20:28.811 --> 20:29.646
Just the two of us?

20:30.480 --> 20:31.731
Why just the two of us?

20:31.814 --> 20:34.025
Did you have something to say to me?

20:34.567 --> 20:35.401
Yes.

20:36.235 --> 20:37.236
I must say something to you.

20:37.904 --> 20:38.988
What should I do?

20:42.075 --> 20:43.201
Here?

20:44.577 --> 20:46.329
We can go somewhere else if you'd like.

20:46.412 --> 20:48.289
No, it's fine.

20:48.873 --> 20:49.999
Please, go ahead.

20:51.292 --> 20:52.543
Ms. Cha,

20:53.503 --> 20:54.379
I like you.

20:54.879 --> 20:55.755
I like you.

20:55.838 --> 20:56.965
I like you.

20:57.048 --> 20:58.800
He's really asking me out?

20:58.883 --> 21:02.178
That's why I'd like for us to go…

21:03.388 --> 21:04.722
Go…

21:06.432 --> 21:09.394
out…

21:10.019 --> 21:12.605
…work together on a task
assigned by the President.

21:13.648 --> 21:14.565
Huh?

21:14.649 --> 21:18.236
A task force is being formed to develop
a new sphere ice refrigerator.

21:18.319 --> 21:20.321
I'd like you on the team, Ms. Cha.

21:27.370 --> 21:28.329
No, please.

21:28.413 --> 21:30.081
I got it. Let me.

21:33.418 --> 21:35.795
I wish I could disappear right now.

21:40.258 --> 21:41.467
Thank you.

21:47.932 --> 21:51.769
So when you said you were fired…

21:51.853 --> 21:53.521
I did get fired from Planning Team 2.

21:53.604 --> 21:54.439
So…

21:54.981 --> 21:56.190
when you wanted to meet

21:56.941 --> 21:58.401
for a drink last weekend…

21:58.484 --> 22:00.445
I wanted to tell you then,
but you were too drunk.

22:00.528 --> 22:01.738
And you kept

22:01.821 --> 22:04.615
following me around today and yesterday…

22:04.699 --> 22:06.492
So that I could have a chance to tell you.

22:09.412 --> 22:10.621
It's absolutely mortifying

22:11.414 --> 22:13.041
that it was all in my head, but…

22:16.210 --> 22:17.128
What a relief.

22:17.837 --> 22:19.547
Thank you for the offer,

22:20.173 --> 22:23.718
but I have no intentions
of changing teams right now.

22:23.801 --> 22:25.762
May I ask why that is?

22:25.845 --> 22:29.640
The voice-activated water dispenser
I'm working on have some issues.

22:30.224 --> 22:32.018
I really want to get it sorted out

22:32.101 --> 22:34.437
and get it launched this year.

22:34.520 --> 22:38.483
If that's the case, I'll make sure you can
stay in the loop until its launch.

22:38.566 --> 22:39.901
No.

22:41.069 --> 22:43.821
If I'm being more honest…

22:45.073 --> 22:46.616
I'm scared of failure right now.

22:48.743 --> 22:50.995
I want to take on something
with a higher chance of success.

22:54.123 --> 22:55.500
I know it wasn't an easy offer to make.

22:56.751 --> 22:57.835
I'm sorry.

22:59.796 --> 23:00.755
I understand.

23:01.964 --> 23:04.967
Please keep this confidential
until the official announcement.

23:05.051 --> 23:05.885
Sure.

23:07.136 --> 23:08.221
Oh, my.

23:08.304 --> 23:10.306
Gosh, I'm so sorry.

23:10.973 --> 23:13.184
Here, I got you new ones.

23:16.979 --> 23:19.524
-Let me pour you a drink, Mr. Kang.
-Thanks.

23:21.609 --> 23:23.653
Actually, I wanted to ask you something.

23:23.736 --> 23:24.904
Go ahead.

23:24.987 --> 23:26.948
Do you know about your nickname?

23:27.031 --> 23:27.907
Hey.

23:29.283 --> 23:30.118
Are you drunk?

23:30.785 --> 23:31.619
No.

23:31.702 --> 23:33.079
"Three-No-Man," right?

23:33.788 --> 23:34.747
So you knew.

23:34.831 --> 23:36.499
"No smile, no people, no sorry."

23:37.291 --> 23:40.128
Whoever came up with that name
did a pretty good job.

23:42.505 --> 23:43.339
So he knew?

23:45.967 --> 23:48.845
Enjoy yourselves and pay with this.

23:48.928 --> 23:50.263
You're leaving already?

23:50.346 --> 23:51.180
Yes.

23:52.140 --> 23:53.432
We had a good talk thanks to you.

23:54.350 --> 23:55.226
See you tomorrow.

23:56.477 --> 23:57.311
Oh, well…

23:57.395 --> 23:58.646
Yes, okay.

23:59.230 --> 24:00.940
Have a safe trip home.

24:02.441 --> 24:03.442
Man.

24:04.610 --> 24:08.114
How dare you use work as an excuse
to drag me out here?

24:08.197 --> 24:09.991
What was I supposed to do?
He said he had to see you.

24:10.074 --> 24:11.868
Man, that hurts!

24:13.661 --> 24:15.204
So what did you talk about?

24:15.288 --> 24:16.914
It's classified, you idiot.

24:18.082 --> 24:19.208
"Classified"?

24:43.316 --> 24:44.942
YEONG-MOOK REPAIR SERVICES

25:02.585 --> 25:03.419
Hi.

25:05.546 --> 25:07.173
-When did you get back?
-A few days ago.

25:08.591 --> 25:11.802
I thought you weren't
coming back for good.

25:16.390 --> 25:17.225
What's that?

25:17.808 --> 25:18.768
I stumbled upon it.

25:26.150 --> 25:27.068
Huh?

25:31.822 --> 25:32.740
My goodness.

25:35.243 --> 25:37.870
I'd have to work another ten years
to get your money's worth.

25:37.954 --> 25:39.538
I'll stumble upon another one
for you in ten years.

25:44.460 --> 25:45.670
Thank you.

26:02.353 --> 26:06.941
Wow, nothing beats
the sound of your audio setup.

26:07.024 --> 26:08.276
What? You're being silly.

26:10.611 --> 26:13.364
It's just a bunch of broken parts
slapped together.

26:13.447 --> 26:14.282
I like it.

26:14.991 --> 26:16.784
Your sound, this shop.

26:18.327 --> 26:19.704
Somehow, I always feel at ease

26:20.871 --> 26:22.039
whenever I come here.

26:22.123 --> 26:23.499
What is it this time?

26:25.126 --> 26:26.127
Something not going well?

26:26.711 --> 26:27.670
How did you know?

26:27.753 --> 26:29.547
You wouldn't be here for any other reason.

26:40.433 --> 26:42.351
There's a mountain of stuff to fix,

26:43.811 --> 26:46.981
so get your hands moving
and sort your head out.

27:08.502 --> 27:10.629
Wow, this one's way too difficult.

27:10.713 --> 27:13.215
You have to try the hard ones
if you want to get better.

27:20.306 --> 27:21.807
Your hands have really slowed down.

27:22.433 --> 27:23.309
Here, let me.

27:23.392 --> 27:24.518
Hey, hey.

27:25.394 --> 27:26.520
Work on your own thing.

27:26.604 --> 27:28.064
I like things with clear solutions.

27:30.983 --> 27:33.819
And that's why you're bad at dating.

27:33.903 --> 27:35.571
Wow, straight for the jugular.

27:36.322 --> 27:37.907
I actually just got rejected, you know.

27:39.658 --> 27:40.910
You have feelings for someone?

27:40.993 --> 27:43.871
Just give me some advice
on what to do in a situation like this.

27:43.954 --> 27:45.748
What advice is there to give?

27:46.540 --> 27:49.752
Either give up completely,
or keep going until it works out.

27:51.587 --> 27:52.421
Is she pretty?

27:55.466 --> 27:56.384
Good.

27:57.218 --> 27:59.929
Hey, smile like that more often.

28:00.846 --> 28:02.556
I now realize at my age

28:03.599 --> 28:05.643
that days you spend smiling
are rare and precious.

28:38.384 --> 28:40.010
Hey, it's a task force announcement!

28:40.094 --> 28:41.887
-What?
-A task force?

28:41.971 --> 28:43.055
What kind of task force?

28:43.139 --> 28:44.849
TASK FORCE: A TEMPORARY TEAM
FORMED FOR A SPECIFIC PROJECT

28:44.932 --> 28:46.684
Why a task force, all of a sudden?

28:47.268 --> 28:48.644
RECRUITMENT - FUTURE STRATEGY TASK FORCE

28:49.019 --> 28:49.854
Manager Kang Si-woo?

28:50.813 --> 28:53.566
So this is what Mr. Kang
was talking about.

28:53.649 --> 28:56.652
He just became Team 2's team lead,
and now he's leading a task force?

29:01.323 --> 29:02.158
Is this why

29:02.241 --> 29:03.742
Mr. Kang asked to see you separately?

29:04.577 --> 29:05.953
-Yeah.
-Did you say yes?

29:06.370 --> 29:07.329
No.

29:07.413 --> 29:08.539
Thank goodness.

29:09.039 --> 29:12.209
I was scared
you were jumping into hell because of me.

29:12.293 --> 29:13.335
What's going on?

29:13.419 --> 29:16.505
Don't keep it between yourselves.
Fill us in. What's happening?

29:21.927 --> 29:24.013
We all thought Mr. Kang was done for

29:24.763 --> 29:27.141
after he talked
about suspending everything,

29:27.224 --> 29:29.226
-did we not?
-Yes.

29:29.310 --> 29:31.020
Well, that was not the case.

29:32.188 --> 29:33.522
As I expected, Mr. Kang,

29:35.149 --> 29:37.318
your current position
isn't right for you at all.

29:39.778 --> 29:42.573
You should step down
from the team lead of Planning Team 2.

29:45.534 --> 29:46.494
As you suggested,

29:47.328 --> 29:50.039
we'll suspend
the sphere ice refrigerator project.

29:50.122 --> 29:50.956
Instead,

29:51.040 --> 29:55.169
you'll form a task force
and start over from scratch.

29:55.794 --> 30:00.132
In that case, I'd like full authority
and responsibility over every stage,

30:00.716 --> 30:01.675
from planning to launch.

30:02.343 --> 30:05.012
And I'll report to you directly.

30:06.472 --> 30:07.348
Let's do it.

30:10.100 --> 30:11.727
Wow, that's insane.

30:12.228 --> 30:13.354
Report directly?

30:14.271 --> 30:18.442
Just how much does the President
trust Mr. Kang to back him this hard?

30:18.526 --> 30:19.902
You know what she's like.

30:19.985 --> 30:20.945
Don't you?

30:21.862 --> 30:24.156
She's a legend who started
as a regular employee

30:24.240 --> 30:26.033
and made it all the way to President.

30:26.116 --> 30:27.785
She knows better than anyone

30:27.868 --> 30:30.329
how rigid hierarchy serves
as a barrier for the employees.

30:32.623 --> 30:34.583
And Mr. Kang picked up on that perfectly.

30:35.834 --> 30:36.752
But

30:36.835 --> 30:39.463
handling a project
that already got suspended once…

30:40.047 --> 30:41.340
Is that a step up or step down?

30:41.423 --> 30:44.218
And that is the main question

30:45.469 --> 30:46.512
for this reorganization.

30:47.680 --> 30:50.724
Did she just give Mr. Kang wings to fly

30:50.808 --> 30:52.184
or set him up for a trap?

30:52.685 --> 30:53.978
Who would even join him then?

30:54.061 --> 30:56.313
Mr. Kang's already hard to deal with,
and if the project fails,

30:56.397 --> 30:57.565
the cost of it would be too much.

30:57.648 --> 31:00.025
Bingo. Great point, No-ah.

31:00.109 --> 31:02.027
So now, what are we supposed to do?

31:02.111 --> 31:03.487
We do absolutely nothing

31:04.363 --> 31:05.489
unless we're told otherwise.

31:06.490 --> 31:09.785
Stay perfectly still.

31:09.868 --> 31:11.495
That is the answer.

31:12.997 --> 31:14.039
Okay?

31:15.708 --> 31:17.293
Mr. Kang is coming over.

31:17.376 --> 31:18.210
Hello!

31:23.048 --> 31:23.882
Oh, wait.

31:30.389 --> 31:32.474
TECH NECK POSTURE
TECH NECK WARNING!

31:38.272 --> 31:40.816
He went and snatched my project
just like that?

31:42.067 --> 31:45.487
No one on this team
is applying for the task force.

31:45.571 --> 31:47.197
That would be an act of betrayal.

31:47.281 --> 31:48.949
-Understood?
-Yes, sir.

31:49.033 --> 31:50.200
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

31:56.582 --> 31:58.500
-Ms. Cha.
-Yes?

31:58.584 --> 32:00.294
How's the water dispenser issue going?

32:00.377 --> 32:02.004
We're testing it
after replacing the microphone.

32:02.588 --> 32:05.007
You have to go and check it yourself.

32:05.090 --> 32:08.093
If that goes wrong too,
we're really done for!

32:08.594 --> 32:09.428
Yes, sir.

32:10.888 --> 32:11.722
Tell me.

32:12.556 --> 32:15.392
Do you think the work
you're assigned to is insignificant?

32:17.353 --> 32:19.938
Sir, I'm heading down
to check on the test.

32:20.022 --> 32:21.690
Even the smallest screw

32:21.774 --> 32:24.193
can bring the whole thing down
if it's not fastened right.

32:24.276 --> 32:26.070
Please do your work
with some self-respect.

32:27.029 --> 32:28.197
Are you crying right now?

32:29.073 --> 32:30.032
No, sir.

32:36.497 --> 32:37.331
Hold it in.

32:37.414 --> 32:38.832
There's no room for tears at work.

33:01.188 --> 33:03.107
Thank goodness I didn't join his team.

33:08.153 --> 33:09.613
TASK FORCE RECRUITMENT STATUS

33:09.697 --> 33:10.948
THERE ARE NO APPLICANTS

33:16.495 --> 33:19.039
-A walk-off home run!
-It's out of here!

33:19.123 --> 33:21.500
The stadium is buzzing
with the fans' cheers.

33:21.583 --> 33:22.876
Hey Buddy,

33:22.960 --> 33:24.628
gimme 100 mil o' cold water, will ya?

33:24.712 --> 33:26.922
A very good swing,
looking for the outside fastball.

33:27.005 --> 33:28.924
Dispensing 100 milliliters of cold water.

33:29.007 --> 33:30.968
What a massive swing that was.

33:31.051 --> 33:31.969
It worked!

33:33.137 --> 33:35.681
It's handling regional dialects
and everyday noise just fine.

33:35.764 --> 33:37.015
Exactly.

33:37.099 --> 33:39.393
But how did the Product Planning Team know

33:39.476 --> 33:41.353
to recommend
this cost-effective microphone?

33:41.937 --> 33:43.689
It's like you always said,

33:43.772 --> 33:45.566
the Product Planning Team

33:45.649 --> 33:48.652
should always keep
a few extra bullets to spare.

33:49.236 --> 33:51.655
And you prepared a backup
as part of those extra bullets?

33:51.739 --> 33:54.283
If I don't have a Plan B ready
ahead of time,

33:54.908 --> 33:56.160
I can't clock out early.

33:56.243 --> 33:57.286
Right. Perfect answer.

33:58.495 --> 34:02.249
Oh, I heard the sphere ice refrigerator
is going to be a task force project.

34:02.332 --> 34:03.834
Yes, correct.

34:06.628 --> 34:08.422
When I saw Mr. Kang
at the Gwangju factory,

34:08.505 --> 34:10.424
I had a feeling
he wouldn't just let it slide.

34:12.009 --> 34:15.387
I heard Mr. Kang used to be
on the Development Team.

34:16.138 --> 34:17.806
What was he like when he was on the team?

34:17.890 --> 34:20.851
He was the same,
never smiling and never talking.

34:20.934 --> 34:23.270
Still, everyone respected him

34:23.353 --> 34:25.981
because Kang Si-woo
never lost against a machine.

34:30.736 --> 34:32.821
I'll let you know
once the final test results are out.

34:33.405 --> 34:34.615
Great, good luck.

34:34.698 --> 34:35.783
Bye.

34:41.955 --> 34:43.081
Mr. Ko.

34:43.165 --> 34:43.999
What is it?

34:44.792 --> 34:47.211
I'd like to take the day off tomorrow.

34:48.796 --> 34:50.547
You're requesting leave for the next day

34:50.631 --> 34:52.382
when the workday's almost over?

34:52.466 --> 34:54.259
What fresh nonsense is this?

34:55.636 --> 34:57.054
I'm sorry, sir.

34:58.096 --> 35:00.891
My sister got hospitalized
all of a sudden.

35:00.974 --> 35:03.060
But why are you taking a day off

35:03.143 --> 35:04.853
when it's your sister
who's in the hospital?

35:06.313 --> 35:07.189
Huh?

35:11.527 --> 35:12.903
Times have changed so much

35:13.445 --> 35:16.281
I'm not even allowed to say anything
about last-minute requests now.

35:17.616 --> 35:18.575
Fine, do it.

35:19.409 --> 35:20.577
Thank you, sir.

35:23.080 --> 35:24.289
Ms. Cha.

35:25.374 --> 35:26.500
Yes?

35:26.583 --> 35:28.794
Take over No-ah's overseas market research

35:28.877 --> 35:30.420
and get it done by tomorrow.

35:30.504 --> 35:32.506
No, I can finish that when I get ba--

35:32.589 --> 35:33.715
It's urgent.

35:35.801 --> 35:37.427
No. I'll just…

35:37.511 --> 35:38.679
Okay, sir.

35:38.762 --> 35:40.055
I'll do it.

35:43.475 --> 35:45.894
Just send me the file,
and I'll handle the rest.

35:46.520 --> 35:47.604
I'm sorry, Ms. Cha.

35:47.688 --> 35:50.315
It's okay.
He's doing that on purpose anyway.

35:53.068 --> 35:55.320
All right.
What are you all doing? Go home!

35:58.907 --> 35:59.741
OVERSEAS MARKET RESEARCH REPORT

35:59.825 --> 36:01.869
EMAIL: CHA JI-YOON

36:03.412 --> 36:05.581
You should go too, No-ah.
Your sister's waiting.

36:19.344 --> 36:20.429
Love is

36:21.763 --> 36:22.848
so selfish

36:24.141 --> 36:25.309
and foolish.

36:29.855 --> 36:31.189
This is the first overtime in a while.

36:39.907 --> 36:41.867
Dear passengers, welcome aboard.

36:42.576 --> 36:46.330
This is the high-speed train
bound for Pohang Station.

36:47.289 --> 36:51.043
Our crew is committed to making sure

36:51.126 --> 36:52.878
you have a comfortable journey.

36:54.129 --> 36:56.298
This train will be departing shortly.

36:56.381 --> 36:57.716
What time do you get off today?

36:57.799 --> 37:00.594
You get off late on Tuesdays, right?
I'm going--

37:04.181 --> 37:07.643
WHAT TIME DO YOU GET OFF TODAY?
YOU GET OFF LATE ON TUESDAYS, RIGHT?

37:14.149 --> 37:15.484
Everything will be fine.

37:17.110 --> 37:20.948
POHAN UNIVERSITY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY

37:21.031 --> 37:23.951
Come on, we're not going if you're not.
Right, guys?

37:24.034 --> 37:25.619
In that case, let me think about--

37:34.753 --> 37:36.380
Do you know her?

37:36.463 --> 37:38.548
Yeah. Why don't you head out first?

38:03.824 --> 38:05.784
You can't just come here
without telling me.

38:05.867 --> 38:06.743
Why not?

38:07.411 --> 38:08.745
Am I not allowed to be here?

38:08.829 --> 38:11.415
That's not what I meant!
I told you I was busy.

38:11.498 --> 38:12.374
I know.

38:12.457 --> 38:14.001
So busy you can't even reply to me

38:14.084 --> 38:15.877
or come to Seoul on the weekends.

38:15.961 --> 38:18.588
That's why I'm here.
Why are you getting so worked up?

38:25.429 --> 38:26.346
I'm sorry.

38:27.723 --> 38:29.725
I just have too much on my plate lately

38:30.350 --> 38:31.810
that I've been really on edge.

38:32.686 --> 38:35.605
I just feel bad that you have to
come to Pohang all the time

38:36.648 --> 38:37.482
when you have work too.

38:39.109 --> 38:41.445
I took tomorrow off to come here
only to get yelled at.

38:42.070 --> 38:42.904
Sorry.

38:43.780 --> 38:45.699
-You haven't eaten, right?
-No.

38:45.782 --> 38:47.576
I'll treat you to something nice.

38:47.659 --> 38:49.202
It'd better be really nice.

39:51.765 --> 39:54.101
Still, everyone respected him

39:54.184 --> 39:57.312
because Kang Si-woo
never lost against a machine.

40:33.640 --> 40:36.768
A boss who's smart and competent.

40:40.605 --> 40:42.315
He's exactly that type of boss.

40:53.076 --> 40:54.369
CHO GA-EUL

41:02.919 --> 41:03.753
MISSED CALL
CHO GA-EUL

41:08.925 --> 41:09.759
Ji-yoon!

41:16.850 --> 41:18.226
I missed you.

41:21.855 --> 41:22.856
What are you doing here?

41:23.440 --> 41:25.150
This trip ran a bit long, didn't it?

41:29.029 --> 41:31.031
I see you're really mad. I'm sorry.

41:31.114 --> 41:34.451
Isn't that something you say when you're
10, 20 minutes late to meet someone?

41:35.535 --> 41:38.413
How could you say that
when you disappeared for eight months?

41:38.496 --> 41:41.041
Did you really think
you could just say, "I'm back,"

41:41.124 --> 41:43.084
and I'd go, "Welcome home,"
like nothing happened?

41:44.502 --> 41:46.129
-Did I make you wait too long?
-Yeah.

41:46.504 --> 41:48.256
At first, I waited out of worry.

41:48.340 --> 41:50.634
Then I waited out of anger.

41:50.717 --> 41:53.094
Then I waited
so I can end things properly.

41:54.054 --> 41:57.098
I waited for you while imagining
this moment over and over again,

41:58.016 --> 41:59.893
yet you show up smiling
like you were only gone

42:01.478 --> 42:02.771
for a couple of days.

42:03.355 --> 42:05.148
How could we break up?

42:05.232 --> 42:07.442
I can't break up with you, Ji-yoon.

42:08.318 --> 42:10.612
Let's go inside.
I have so much to tell you.

42:14.241 --> 42:15.742
I said this over text too,

42:17.244 --> 42:18.787
but I wanted to say it at least once

42:19.663 --> 42:20.914
right to your face.

42:22.332 --> 42:23.625
Cho Ga-eul.

42:24.834 --> 42:26.169
It's already over between us.

42:26.920 --> 42:29.005
Ji-yoon. Ji-yoon!

42:29.089 --> 42:31.132
You should've just never returned!

42:31.216 --> 42:32.509
Why did you come back?

42:35.845 --> 42:37.430
Because I left something important behind.

42:39.724 --> 42:41.268
And I can't live without it.

42:43.103 --> 42:45.021
YEAR 2021

42:45.105 --> 42:46.106
Hi.

42:46.189 --> 42:47.190
Ga-eul.

42:48.358 --> 42:49.901
How have you been?

42:56.032 --> 42:57.325
When did you get back from Australia?

42:59.327 --> 43:00.620
It's been ages.

43:01.371 --> 43:04.291
I contacted you as soon as I got back,
but you'd changed your number.

43:04.374 --> 43:06.543
I changed it
when I got a new phone from work.

43:06.626 --> 43:08.712
You changed
after you started working there.

43:08.795 --> 43:11.589
We used to stay in touch
all the time before that.

43:15.176 --> 43:16.219
It doesn't matter.

43:16.803 --> 43:18.221
I'm just glad we met like this.

43:20.724 --> 43:22.642
I guess we really are meant to be.

43:23.226 --> 43:25.145
Don't make jokes like that anymore.

43:27.480 --> 43:29.858
You know I had feelings for you
for a long time.

43:31.484 --> 43:34.154
Do you know how hard it was
to get over you?

43:37.240 --> 43:38.325
Then will you be my girlfriend?

43:41.453 --> 43:42.329
What?

43:43.079 --> 43:45.206
Be my girlfriend, Ji-yoon.

43:46.833 --> 43:47.792
Do you…

43:52.047 --> 43:53.757
Do you like me?

43:55.884 --> 43:56.968
Yeah.

43:57.594 --> 43:59.179
Not as a friend.

43:59.262 --> 44:00.096
Yeah,

44:00.638 --> 44:01.848
I like you romantically.

44:01.931 --> 44:03.099
Since when?

44:04.100 --> 44:07.103
With music-making and Australia,
you wouldn't have had time for that.

44:09.230 --> 44:10.565
I've liked you in between things.

44:11.066 --> 44:11.900
What?

44:12.484 --> 44:13.735
In between working,

44:14.819 --> 44:16.363
in between writing songs,

44:17.405 --> 44:18.907
in between zoning out…

44:21.117 --> 44:22.660
I kept thinking of you,

44:23.661 --> 44:26.081
like I'd left something important behind.

44:27.582 --> 44:28.792
In between moments like that,

44:30.085 --> 44:31.211
and for a very long time.

44:32.629 --> 44:35.298
I like you, Ji-yoon.

44:58.238 --> 44:59.906
Take it all. Everything you left behind.

45:00.490 --> 45:02.325
That's not what I meant
by something I left behind.

45:02.409 --> 45:03.243
You know that.

45:03.827 --> 45:05.662
Whatever, then.
Throw it out for all I care.

45:07.580 --> 45:08.498
I'm sorry

45:09.249 --> 45:10.458
for taking this long.

45:13.044 --> 45:14.129
At that point,

45:15.296 --> 45:17.173
you'd basically forgotten me.

45:18.508 --> 45:19.926
For me,

45:21.094 --> 45:22.345
it was painful,

45:22.429 --> 45:24.055
but it was enough time
for me to get over you.

45:26.433 --> 45:28.351
So don't show up
out of the blue like this again.

45:29.102 --> 45:30.895
I'm not happy to see you anymore.

45:32.772 --> 45:33.731
Ji-yoon.

46:40.131 --> 46:41.174
Hello.

46:45.220 --> 46:46.679
You paid and didn't take this
the other day.

46:47.347 --> 46:49.432
Oh, right. That's okay.

46:49.516 --> 46:50.433
Did you not get it?

46:51.100 --> 46:53.895
I gave it to one of our regulars
who was with you that day.

46:56.064 --> 46:58.608
Here's the overseas market report
that No-ah was working on.

47:00.610 --> 47:03.029
And this is the revised
profit-and-loss simulation

47:03.112 --> 47:04.239
after replacing the microphone.

47:06.866 --> 47:07.951
The microphone…

47:08.993 --> 47:10.453
Let's go with the original one.

47:11.663 --> 47:12.497
Pardon?

47:12.580 --> 47:14.624
I thought it over all night,

47:14.707 --> 47:17.585
and replacing the microphone
feels like a rash decision.

47:18.628 --> 47:21.381
The risk is too high,
so let's just stick to the old one.

47:21.464 --> 47:23.841
But we already completed
the first test yesterday,

47:24.592 --> 47:26.135
and the final test is today.

47:26.803 --> 47:28.429
Then just go and stop it.

47:29.597 --> 47:30.473
Sir.

47:31.099 --> 47:32.058
What the heck?

47:34.769 --> 47:36.521
Are you rebelling right now, Ms. Cha?

47:37.981 --> 47:38.856
That's not it.

47:40.525 --> 47:43.278
But what about
the voice recognition errors?

47:43.361 --> 47:47.198
Tell them to keep the microphone
and just fix the software!

47:47.282 --> 47:49.409
But that won't fix the problem.

47:49.492 --> 47:51.327
And why is that your concern?

47:51.411 --> 47:52.829
You're not an engineer, Ms. Cha.

47:53.621 --> 47:55.665
Just go and pass along the message.

47:58.084 --> 47:59.502
Sir, please reconsider…

48:02.380 --> 48:04.007
If you can't do it, I'll go myself.

48:05.675 --> 48:06.509
Sir.

48:06.884 --> 48:07.802
Sir!

48:08.469 --> 48:10.513
Please think it over one more time.

48:11.180 --> 48:13.725
The Development Team
ran tests all night for several days.

48:13.808 --> 48:15.977
That's what those people are there for.

48:17.020 --> 48:18.104
What the hell? Move!

48:18.187 --> 48:19.522
You haven't changed a bit.

48:19.606 --> 48:20.481
What?

48:20.565 --> 48:22.900
Looks like you had
an expensive dinner last night.

48:27.196 --> 48:28.197
Why this…

48:29.240 --> 48:30.325
Darn it.

48:47.925 --> 48:49.218
What did you do with my drink?

48:49.719 --> 48:50.553
Sorry?

48:54.057 --> 48:55.767
Oh, from the convenience store?

48:55.850 --> 48:56.934
Did you drink it?

48:57.018 --> 48:58.645
No, it's in my fridge at home.

48:58.728 --> 49:00.730
Then I'll come by your place
after work to get it.

49:02.649 --> 49:04.025
I can buy you the same one.

49:04.108 --> 49:05.193
No.

49:05.276 --> 49:07.111
Then I'll bring it to you tomor--

49:07.195 --> 49:08.821
I have to drink it today.

49:12.492 --> 49:13.326
Sure.

49:31.511 --> 49:34.931
You do know
that was completely unreasonable, right?

49:37.809 --> 49:39.977
You would've just avoided me
if I'd asked to meet.

49:43.272 --> 49:45.024
What happened
with that ordeal from earlier?

49:45.108 --> 49:48.027
The Development Team made a huge fuss,

49:48.736 --> 49:52.657
but then everything just went back
to normal like nothing had happened.

49:59.914 --> 50:01.165
Something similar happened

50:01.916 --> 50:03.376
back when I was a Sr. Associate.

50:04.836 --> 50:06.129
Mr. Ko was the team lead,

50:06.713 --> 50:10.216
and he suddenly decided to replace
a faultless part with another supplier's.

50:10.633 --> 50:11.467
When I looked into it,

50:12.760 --> 50:14.220
I found signs he'd accepted favors.

50:16.806 --> 50:18.891
Kang was still a Sr. Associate,
and get this,

50:18.975 --> 50:22.478
he actually reported his team lead,
Mr. Ko, for bribery,

50:23.354 --> 50:25.064
just so he could take that spot.

50:25.732 --> 50:27.817
So what did you do then?

50:27.900 --> 50:29.902
I reported it to the Internal Audit Team.

50:30.653 --> 50:32.196
There was no conclusive evidence,

50:32.905 --> 50:35.700
so they just kept the original supplier
and closed the case.

50:36.492 --> 50:39.704
And I got kicked out
of the Product Planning Team.

50:43.666 --> 50:44.959
That must have been hard.

50:45.793 --> 50:47.003
That's when I decided

50:48.087 --> 50:50.715
I'd stop dealing in politics
and let my work speak for itself.

50:53.176 --> 50:54.218
Join the task force.

50:54.844 --> 50:56.971
I won't let something like this
happen to you again.

50:57.889 --> 50:59.849
Why are you doing all this for me?

51:00.892 --> 51:02.852
We haven't even
known each other that long.

51:05.188 --> 51:06.272
I've been watching you

51:07.982 --> 51:08.816
for a long time.

51:15.990 --> 51:17.033
Hello!

51:17.116 --> 51:18.534
My name is Cha Ji-yoon.

51:20.036 --> 51:23.623
One day, I want to create
an automated magical homemaker system

51:23.706 --> 51:25.958
that does the cleaning,
dishes, and laundry

51:26.042 --> 51:28.586
all on its own before we even ask!

51:28.669 --> 51:30.797
SAEUM NEW HIRE ORIENTATION

51:30.880 --> 51:31.923
What's your ultimate goal?

51:32.006 --> 51:35.176
Obviously,
becoming the President of SAEUM!

51:39.138 --> 51:42.099
One new hire's ambitious goal
made a strong impression on me.

51:42.975 --> 51:44.936
Still, like most rookies,

51:45.019 --> 51:46.938
I figured it wouldn't last long.

51:47.021 --> 51:50.024
What if there were
a talking robot vacuum companion?

51:50.107 --> 51:53.486
If we combine a robot vacuum cleaner
with a voice assistant service,

51:53.569 --> 51:55.863
it could evolve
into a talking robot vacuum cleaner.

51:55.947 --> 51:58.407
Users could give it
a name of their choice,

51:58.491 --> 52:00.952
and whenever they have a question
or need someone to talk to,

52:01.035 --> 52:03.246
they could just
talk to their robot vacuum cleaner.

52:03.913 --> 52:06.749
"Bokja, will it stop raining tomorrow?"

52:08.000 --> 52:10.294
Wait, is "Bokja" too tacky?

52:10.378 --> 52:12.171
But that rookie was different.

52:12.964 --> 52:15.758
She knew exactly what she wanted to do.

52:17.760 --> 52:18.719
Seriously, enough already.

52:18.803 --> 52:19.971
It may be a machine,

52:20.054 --> 52:22.723
but it has to feel like it has emotions.

52:26.185 --> 52:27.103
Please.

52:30.940 --> 52:33.693
Her ambition didn't waver
even as the years passed,

52:33.776 --> 52:35.236
and I quietly rooted for her.

52:37.321 --> 52:39.866
But when I saw you again at the factory,

52:39.949 --> 52:41.158
you'd changed a lot.

52:41.742 --> 52:45.788
-…and gradually improve it step by step?
-Honestly,

52:45.913 --> 52:46.956
I was disappointed.

52:47.915 --> 52:49.333
Then I saw your notebook and realized.

52:50.334 --> 52:51.252
You didn't change.

52:51.794 --> 52:52.920
You were just hiding.

52:54.213 --> 52:55.631
For the first time, I thought,

52:55.715 --> 52:58.342
"I don't want to let this person go."

53:00.011 --> 53:02.430
If you ask me, you're good enough

53:02.513 --> 53:04.682
to allow yourself to aim much higher.

53:05.766 --> 53:07.810
It'd be a waste to keep your potential

53:08.436 --> 53:11.063
hidden away in a notebook like that.

53:13.816 --> 53:15.067
I'll give you some time to think.

53:18.112 --> 53:19.280
And thank you

53:20.072 --> 53:21.407
for holding on to my drink.

53:33.961 --> 53:34.795
What was that?

53:37.965 --> 53:39.425
That's more exciting than asking me out.

53:41.719 --> 53:44.680
Butterflies… I feel butterflies.

54:08.329 --> 54:09.497
She must've run here.

54:22.802 --> 54:25.638
Babe, when we get married,
should I move down here?

54:26.722 --> 54:27.974
What about your job?

54:28.557 --> 54:30.184
I could move to another company,

54:30.267 --> 54:31.686
or try to get a public-sector job.

54:32.645 --> 54:35.189
Come on, why would you leave a big company

54:35.272 --> 54:36.649
everyone's dying to get into?

54:37.650 --> 54:40.653
But you won't be able to move to Seoul
right after you get your degree.

54:40.736 --> 54:43.864
What's the point of getting married
if we still can't see each other often?

54:48.911 --> 54:50.413
You're going to be late for school.

54:50.496 --> 54:51.956
You should get going.

54:54.625 --> 54:55.459
See you.

55:01.716 --> 55:02.675
No-ah!

55:06.470 --> 55:07.430
No-ah, let's…

55:07.513 --> 55:11.183
The 559 train bound for Seoul

55:11.267 --> 55:13.310
will be arriving shortly

55:13.394 --> 55:14.478
-at Platform 7.
-…break up.

55:15.396 --> 55:18.482
Please stand behind the yellow line.

55:19.650 --> 55:24.238
Passengers, please check
the car before boarding.

55:49.472 --> 55:50.514
No-ah!

55:51.348 --> 55:52.224
What's wrong?

55:52.308 --> 55:53.684
Oh, no! Gosh.

55:53.768 --> 55:54.685
Are you feeling sick?

55:55.269 --> 55:56.437
Ms. Cha…

55:56.520 --> 55:57.855
Let's get you to the hospital. Get up.

55:58.773 --> 56:01.484
I can't. I already took yesterday off.

56:01.567 --> 56:03.986
You can't work in this state.

56:05.738 --> 56:06.655
What?

56:06.739 --> 56:08.783
She took a day off yesterday

56:08.866 --> 56:10.076
and wants to leave early today?

56:11.368 --> 56:13.496
You see, I wait until after work

56:13.579 --> 56:15.039
or until the weekend to get sick.

56:15.122 --> 56:17.458
Don't you know maintaining yourself
is part of the job?

56:19.126 --> 56:20.044
Ms. Yoon No-ah.

56:22.546 --> 56:23.380
Sir.

56:23.464 --> 56:26.300
Are you even good at anything, Ms. Yoon?

56:26.383 --> 56:27.551
Huh?

56:27.635 --> 56:29.261
You're not quick like Ms. Cha here.

56:29.345 --> 56:30.721
You don't even have any guts either!

56:30.805 --> 56:33.140
No-ah is very unwell right now.

56:33.224 --> 56:35.684
How about we let her go home now
and talk again tomorrow?

56:35.768 --> 56:38.771
I see you're wearing the same clothes
as you did two days ago.

56:39.480 --> 56:43.067
You lied about your sister and went
on a trip with your boyfriend, didn't you?

56:43.150 --> 56:46.195
-Mr. Ko!
-Just go get married then, yeah?

56:46.278 --> 56:48.614
Instead of coming into the office,
being a payroll thief!

56:48.697 --> 56:50.616
That's enough!

56:55.746 --> 56:57.081
Mocking and not recognizing

56:57.164 --> 56:59.625
an employee's performance or abilities
without just cause,

57:00.584 --> 57:03.629
pressuring your employee
not to use vacation or sick leave,

57:04.547 --> 57:06.924
and spreading rumors or insults
about their personal life.

57:07.842 --> 57:10.928
Everything you said to Ms. Yoon just now

57:11.554 --> 57:13.389
falls under workplace harassment.

57:15.641 --> 57:17.518
So what? You're going to report me?

57:17.601 --> 57:19.270
I don't want to do that.

57:20.855 --> 57:22.356
So please…

57:23.816 --> 57:26.318
stop speaking to us so disrespectfully.

57:29.947 --> 57:31.031
Please.

57:39.832 --> 57:41.500
You're full of surprises,

57:42.418 --> 57:43.294
Ms. Cha.

57:47.381 --> 57:48.340
Fine.

57:49.133 --> 57:50.426
So be it, then.

57:50.509 --> 57:51.510
Going forward,

57:51.594 --> 57:54.805
I'll be very polite to you all.

57:57.183 --> 58:00.352
Ms. Yoon No-ah,
since you're unwell, please leave early.

58:01.896 --> 58:02.980
Ms. Cha Ji-yoon.

58:04.732 --> 58:07.067
Please prepare a report
on our competitors' trends

58:07.151 --> 58:09.195
over the past three years.

58:10.112 --> 58:12.072
This is not an unfair assignment,

58:12.156 --> 58:16.577
but a perfectly legitimate request
that is necessary for the team.

58:25.085 --> 58:26.545
Why are you staring like that?

58:42.311 --> 58:44.146
Why would you pick a fight with him?

58:44.230 --> 58:45.189
Ms. Cha.

58:46.440 --> 58:47.316
Let's go.

58:50.527 --> 58:51.570
Go straight to the hospital.

58:51.654 --> 58:53.864
I can't come with you,
so call your sister.

58:54.573 --> 58:56.617
I'm sorry, this is all my fault.

58:56.951 --> 58:59.411
It's not your fault. Now go.

59:39.034 --> 59:40.536
PRODUCT PLANNING TEAM 1
CHA JI-YOON

59:47.584 --> 59:48.836
Mom!

59:49.378 --> 59:51.463
I'm officially starting work tomorrow!

59:51.547 --> 59:53.590
I got assigned
to the Product Planning Team.

59:53.674 --> 59:56.719
My name and photo are right here
on my employee ID!

59:57.303 --> 01:00:00.264
I'm actually at the shop right now
to buy rice cakes for the neighborhood.

01:00:01.223 --> 01:00:03.017
Rice cakes? Why?

01:00:03.100 --> 01:00:05.644
I have to celebrate my daughter
landing a job at a major company!

01:00:06.478 --> 01:00:07.730
Product what team, did you say?

01:00:08.355 --> 01:00:09.898
What will you be doing there?

01:00:09.982 --> 01:00:11.984
You wouldn't understand
even if I told you.

01:00:12.067 --> 01:00:15.821
I'm going to give this job my all.

01:00:15.904 --> 01:00:18.991
I'm going to stay at this company forever.

01:00:19.867 --> 01:00:21.410
I'm on my way home now.

01:00:21.493 --> 01:00:22.578
Let's have a barbecue party!

01:00:56.862 --> 01:00:59.365
COMPETITOR TRENDS REPORT, 2023-2025

01:01:06.080 --> 01:01:08.582
Cha Ji-yoon, Product Planning Team 1.

01:01:08.665 --> 01:01:11.168
Title, Sr. Associate.

01:01:11.251 --> 01:01:13.253
I hereby submit my resignation
for personal reasons…

01:01:13.337 --> 01:01:14.171
RESIGNATION URGE STICKERS

01:01:14.755 --> 01:01:17.466
…and ask that it be processed accordingly.

01:01:21.470 --> 01:01:22.930
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

01:01:23.013 --> 01:01:24.598
"Personal reasons," my ass.

01:01:25.516 --> 01:01:26.975
I may seem

01:01:27.059 --> 01:01:30.479
like nothing more than
some insignificant worker bee to you all,

01:01:30.562 --> 01:01:32.356
but I too am someone

01:01:32.439 --> 01:01:34.942
who joined this company

01:01:35.025 --> 01:01:36.360
with hopes and dreams.

01:01:37.528 --> 01:01:38.487
Tell me.

01:01:38.570 --> 01:01:41.949
Does insulting me,

01:01:42.032 --> 01:01:43.617
looking down on me,

01:01:43.700 --> 01:01:46.662
and treating me like I'm nothing at all
make you feel good?!

01:01:46.745 --> 01:01:48.997
I'm so sick of this place

01:01:49.081 --> 01:01:52.084
that I'm walking out on my own terms!

01:01:53.001 --> 01:01:56.046
You all have a nice life, okay?

01:01:56.130 --> 01:02:00.134
I'm setting off
to find happiness for myself.

01:02:00.217 --> 01:02:02.136
LETTER OF RESIGNATION
CONFIRM SUBMISSION

01:02:06.890 --> 01:02:08.559
SUBMIT THIS DOCUMENT?
CANCEL - CONFIRM

01:02:14.106 --> 01:02:14.940
Darn it.

01:02:27.995 --> 01:02:29.788
You are so sad and pathetic.

01:02:32.374 --> 01:02:33.500
Can't even throw this away?

01:03:16.460 --> 01:03:19.922
HOT AIR UV SYSTEM
SHOE CARE DEVICE

01:03:20.005 --> 01:03:21.507
Reporting from the future.

01:03:21.590 --> 01:03:22.716
This has been released already.

01:03:40.317 --> 01:03:42.194
Washer and dryer combined into one?

01:03:42.778 --> 01:03:44.279
Now it's possible with a single machine.

01:03:45.572 --> 01:03:46.698
How should I open this?

01:03:47.824 --> 01:03:50.035
Touch lightly to automatically open doors.

01:03:51.245 --> 01:03:54.039
Why would he scribble
all over someone else's notebook?

01:03:56.875 --> 01:03:58.794
Did he think using a pencil makes it okay?

01:04:02.548 --> 01:04:05.676
Can't we turn everything into away mode
with one action, like a hotel key card?

01:04:06.426 --> 01:04:07.553
We can.

01:04:07.636 --> 01:04:11.431
You just make a single software
control multiple hardware devices.

01:04:11.515 --> 01:04:15.352
For example, you could make a single phone
control every home appliance.

01:04:20.857 --> 01:04:22.317
Ice spikes?

01:04:29.700 --> 01:04:30.534
Good!

01:04:33.453 --> 01:04:34.621
Mr. Kang…

01:04:36.331 --> 01:04:37.791
What a piece of work.

01:05:03.483 --> 01:05:05.527
LETTER OF RESIGNATION
SUBMIT THIS DOCUMENT?

01:05:20.459 --> 01:05:22.669
SUBMIT THIS DOCUMENT?
CANCEL - CONFIRM

01:05:30.344 --> 01:05:32.095
There's no such thing as the perfect boss.

01:05:34.765 --> 01:05:36.767
Just like there's no such thing
as the perfect partner.

01:05:39.770 --> 01:05:41.313
-Hello.
-Hello.

01:05:45.317 --> 01:05:47.778
…that'll solve everything.

01:05:50.614 --> 01:05:51.907
Good morning, Mr. Ko.

01:05:51.990 --> 01:05:53.909
Why yes, Ms. Cha. Good morning.

01:06:00.165 --> 01:06:01.166
What the…

01:06:01.249 --> 01:06:03.794
At the end of the day,
this is a game of this or that.

01:06:03.877 --> 01:06:05.087
Why's she going over there?

01:06:05.170 --> 01:06:06.046
Hey, wrong way.

01:06:06.129 --> 01:06:07.172
Huh?

01:06:07.255 --> 01:06:10.175
Even if tomorrow's me
regrets the choice I make today…

01:06:10.759 --> 01:06:11.927
What?

01:06:12.010 --> 01:06:13.220
Sr. Associate Cha Ji-yoon,

01:06:13.303 --> 01:06:14.888
here to apply for the task force.

01:06:17.974 --> 01:06:18.975
Wait!

01:06:22.437 --> 01:06:24.231
All I can do is choose

01:06:24.314 --> 01:06:26.483
the second worst, not the worst.

01:06:30.404 --> 01:06:31.405
Nice to work with you.

01:06:35.409 --> 01:06:36.660
Nice to work with you too.

01:07:29.880 --> 01:07:31.381
We have to make

01:07:31.465 --> 01:07:33.633
the perfect sphere ice
with the time we have left.

01:07:33.717 --> 01:07:34.551
Would that be possible?

01:07:34.634 --> 01:07:35.886
Fail. Fail.

01:07:37.596 --> 01:07:38.930
I'm wiped.

01:07:41.308 --> 01:07:42.976
Please get a silent keyboard.

01:07:43.059 --> 01:07:45.812
I'll clock out on time
and order fried chicken no matter what.

01:07:45.896 --> 01:07:47.606
This is uncomfortable as hell.

01:07:48.857 --> 01:07:51.401
I've finally completed our song.

01:07:52.527 --> 01:07:54.738
Would you mind leaving us?

01:07:55.363 --> 01:07:56.740
I have something to tell her too.

01:07:56.823 --> 01:07:59.117
So you'll be free this weekend after all.

01:07:59.201 --> 01:08:00.827
Lovesick?

01:08:05.332 --> 01:08:07.334
Subtitle: Yenny Kang
